Subject: [PATCH] fonts: DirectWrite line gap under a Windows profile

The line gap feeds line-height: normal. FreeType reports hhea's lineGap,
which Windows folds into the win extent for Consolas, Calibri and Segoe
UI (so they have none) and keeps in part for Arial and Times New Roman
(67 and 87 units of 2048). Under a Windows profile the line gap is the
one FontMetrics::WindowsVerticalMetricsFor derives from the tables, as
DirectWrite reports it. Author line-height overrides are unaffected.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/simple_font_data.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/simple_font_data.cc
index 2fa1abf..d9d31f4 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/simple_font_data.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/simple_font_data.cc
@@ -170,6 +170,16 @@ void SimpleFontData::PlatformInit(bool subpixel_ascent_descent,
     line_gap = *metrics_override.line_gap_override * platform_data_->size();
   } else {
     line_gap = metrics.fLeading;
+    // Apostate: under a Windows profile the line gap is the one DirectWrite
+    // reports (FontMetrics::WindowsVerticalMetricsFor), not FreeType's hhea
+    // lineGap: none for Consolas or Calibri, whose hhea gap Windows folds
+    // into the win extent, and the leftover external leading for Arial and
+    // Times New Roman. Author line-height overrides take the branch above.
+    if (const std::optional<FontMetrics::WindowsVerticalMetrics> windows =
+            FontMetrics::WindowsVerticalMetricsFor(*font_.getTypeface(),
+                                                   platform_data_->size())) {
+      line_gap = windows->line_gap;
+    }
   }
   font_metrics_.SetLineGap(line_gap);
   font_metrics_.SetLineSpacing(lroundf(ascent) + lroundf(descent) +
